    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0153" n="79" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg79"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1168.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation Of The United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 15, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In connection with my despatch No. 1164, of
                    the 2d instant, I now have the honor to transmit copies of two more notes which
                    have passed between Lord Clarendon and myself, on the extraordinary position
                    taken by the attorney general in his speech of the 23d of February, in the House
                    of Commons.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C</hi></p>
                </postscript>





